s instead of waiting for the raw three-way spread cure. The READY-gated capture, retention across a compatible reopen, cohort selection, revocation, consumer code, budgets, cadences, the 60-second window and the 120-second barrier are unchanged; nothing derives ACTIVE or READY from nodes.status, publication counts, or coverage. Proven deterministically on the real owner: red on HEAD (no successor, late joiner null), green after.","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"single-seed-minting-authority","statement":"Only the seed's formation-release closure owner mints a successor generation, and only on the evaluation after a captured generation completes, while isRetainableAuthority(authority, completedGeneration) still holds."},{"id":"typed-bounded-admission","statement":"The successor admission is one typed variant (closed | completed_generation) closed by the successor capture, by any revocation, and by the first incompatible or absent authority observation; it never reopens without a new completion; repeated evaluations mint no generation, log no transition and issue no durable write; no candidates means no capture."},{"id":"consumer-validation-unchanged","statement":"A successor captured under the reopen carries the current publication epoch and the completed generation's fence and boot incarnation, is non-authorizing until the durable readback, and is consumed only through the unchanged CONSUMER validation; no consumer/joiner code changes."},{"id":"unchanged-owner-rules","statement":"The READY-gated capture, retention across the compatible reopen, cohort selection from the canonical set, and member-loss/incarnation/substantive-block revocation are byte-for-byte unchanged; budgets, cadences, the 60-second GCP certification window and the 120-second barrier are unchanged; no sleeps."},{"id":"no-second-active-authority","statement":"Do not make the harness, analyzer, or readiness owner derive cluster-ACTIVE or READY from nodes.status, publication counts, or coverage."},{"id":"deterministic-first","statement":"Proof is a deterministic witness on the real closure owner reproducing run 2026-08-30T10-05-10 (reopen observed before gen-1 completes, two pre-ready candidates), red on HEAD (3/8) and green after (8/8), with the pre-reopen sequence and both pair witnesses as controls that must stay green; no GCP run is part of the proof."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"landingRequirements":null,"frontierIds":["formation-release-handoff-post-reopen-capture-main"]}}
